  "stem": "An urgent CT scan is performed, as shown in the accompanying image.\n\nThe scan is reported as showing bilateral non-acute frontal subdural haemorrhages, with no evidence of mass effect or skull fracture.\n\nWhich one of the following is the main significance of this finding?",
  "questionType": "SBA",
  "options": [
    {
      "key": "A",
      "text": "The child does not require neurosurgical intervention",
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "key": "B",
      "text": "This is a potential Non-Accidental Injury",
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "key": "C",
      "text": "The child may have a bleeding disorder",
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "Bilateral non-acute subdural haemorrhages in a child are concerning for non-accidental injury (abusive head trauma) and warrant safeguarding assessment. The absence of mass effect or skull fracture does not remove that concern.",
